<title>USA: White House says no cause for inflation fears.</title>
<headline>White House says no cause for inflation fears.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House Friday hailed the &quot;stunningly good&quot; U.S. unemployment rate, the lowest in more than two decades, and said it offers no inflationary fears.</p>
<p>&quot;It's stunningly good news,&quot; White House Press Secretary Mike McCurry said of Labor Department figures that put the jobless rate at 4.8 percent in May -- its lowest level since October 1973.</p>
<p>&quot;Job creation is not so strong as to cause fears about inflation,&quot; McCurry told reporters.</p>
</text>
